"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[92338],{192338:e=>{e.exports="# How to find resource\n\n## Tools\n\n- **apiGetLakewatchResourceById** — Get any resource by `resourceType` (`datasource` | `rule` | `security-case` | `system-case` | `query`) and `resourceId`. Returns full definition. Use when you already have the ID.\n- **apiListLakewatchDatasources** — List datasources (`thoughts`, `limit`). Use to find a datasource by name, then get by ID.\n- **apiFindLakewatchDetectionRules** — Find or count detection rules by fuzzy name, ID, description, metadata, or SQL text. Builds a compact local search index from cached rule-list pages or paginated API results. Use this for specific rule lookup, filtered counts, and total rule counts. Omit `query` when the user asks for the total number of rules.\n- **apiListLakewatchDetectionRules** — Browse detection rules (`thoughts`, `limit`, optional `cursor`). Use this when the user asks to show/list rules page by page.\n- **apiListLakewatchSecurityCases** — List security cases (`thoughts`, `limit`) with optional filtering (e.g. state, severity as arrays of values, unassigned, ruleId, titleSearch) and sorting. Use to find by name or to answer “open cases”, “high severity”, “unassigned”, etc. See [find-security-case.md](find-security-case.md) for common questions → filter/sort.\n- **apiListLakewatchSystemCases** — List system cases (`thoughts`, `limit`) with optional filtering (e.g. state, severity as arrays of values, resourceType/resourceId) and sorting. Use to find by name or to answer “open alerts”, “alerts for this datasource”, etc. See [find-system-case.md](find-system-case.md) for common questions → filter/sort.\n- **apiListLakewatchSecurityCaseNotables** — List notables (events) for a security case by `caseId`; optional `limit`. See [find-case-events.md](find-case-events.md).\n- **apiListLakewatchSystemCaseEvents** — List events (operational alerts) for a system case by `caseId`; optional `limit`. See [find-case-events.md](find-case-events.md).\n- **apiGetLakewatchManagedTables** — List table names in a medallion layer (`thoughts`, `medallionLayer`: bronze | silver | gold). Use when locating tables via datasource/preset or searching schemas. See [find-table.md](find-table.md).\n- **apiGetLakewatchConfig** — Get workspace config (e.g. catalog and schema names, `spec.systemTablesConfig` for the notables table location). Use with table discovery and for ad-hoc notables queries; see [find-case-events.md](find-case-events.md).\n- **apiListLakewatchDatasourcePresets** / **apiGetLakewatchDatasourcePreset** — List or get presets; presets define tables when a datasource uses one. See [find-table.md](find-table.md).\n- **readTable** / **executeSql** — For notables table schema or ad-hoc queries against `{catalog}.{schema}.notables`; catalog and schema from apiGetLakewatchConfig. See [find-case-events.md](find-case-events.md).\n\n**General flow**: User gives an **ID** → use `apiGetLakewatchResourceById` with the right `resourceType`. User gives a **rule name/description/search phrase** or asks for a **rule count** → use `apiFindLakewatchDetectionRules`, then get by ID if opening one. User asks to browse resources page by page → use the matching **list** tool. **Multiple** matches → present options and ask the user to choose. **None** match → say so and suggest listing all or trying different filters.\n\n## Per-Resource Guides\n\n- **Datasource** — [find-datasource.md](find-datasource.md) (ID prefix `ds-`, list + get by name)\n- **Detection rule** — [find-rule.md](find-rule.md) (ID prefix `rl-`, fuzzy find + get by ID)\n- **Security case** — [find-security-case.md](find-security-case.md) (list with optional filter/sort + get by name/description)\n- **System case** — [find-system-case.md](find-system-case.md) (list with optional filter/sort + get by name/description)\n- **Query** — [find-query.md](find-query.md) (get by ID only; no list tool)\n- **Table** — [find-table.md](find-table.md) (discover by datasource → preset → medallion schema search; no single-ID lookup)\n- **Case events** — [find-case-events.md](find-case-events.md) (list notables for a security case or events for a system case by case ID)\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Identify ID vs. name early** — Datasource IDs start with `ds-`, rule IDs start with `rl-` (random-generated). Names are descriptive, human-readable.\n2. **Flexible name matching** — Account for case, hyphens/underscores/spaces, and partial matches.\n3. **Always get full resource after resolving ID** — Use `apiGetLakewatchResourceById` once you have the ID; list responses may only include summaries.\n4. **Handle ambiguity** — When multiple resources match, present all with distinguishing info and prompt the user to choose.\n5. **Provide context in responses** — When presenting a resource, include name, ID, description, and key config; suggest next steps.\n6. **Confirm navigation** — When found resources, ask user if they wanted to navigate to the resource page if applicable.\n\n## Error Handling\n\n- **Resource ID not found** — The resource may have been deleted, renamed, or not yet created. Offer to list all resources of that type.\n- **No resource matching name** — Say you checked the list and didn’t find a match; suggest listing all, trying a different name, or creating a new one.\n- **API error** — Surface the error message and suggest retrying or contacting support.\n- **Empty workspace** — If there are no datasources or rules, say so and offer to help create the first one.\n\nResource definitions are in the base instructions. For directing the user to a page use **how-to-navigation**.\n"}}]);
